@*
    Shown for the moment it takes to ask the API whether the cookies still name
    a valid session. A quiet holding state, not a spinner on an empty page —
    flashing the sign-in form at someone who is already signed in is worse than
    a brief pause.
*@

<div class="auth-gate">
    <FundMark Size="44" />
    <p>Checking your session</p>
</div>

<style>
    .auth-gate {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: var(--s-4);
        min-height: 100dvh;
        color: var(--ink-4);
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
        animation: gate-in 400ms var(--ease) 180ms both;
    }

    /* Delayed so a fast answer never flashes this on screen at all. */
    @@keyframes gate-in {
        from { opacity: 0; }
        to   { opacity: 1; }
    }
</style>
